# Dropdown Components

## Multi-Level Dropdown Components

### Basic Dropdown with Search
```typescript
import {
  DropdownMenu,
  DropdownMenuContent,
  DropdownMenuGroup,
  DropdownMenuItem,
  DropdownMenuLabel,
  DropdownMenuSeparator,
  DropdownMenuTrigger,
  DropdownMenuSub,
  DropdownMenuSubContent,
  DropdownMenuSubTrigger,
  DropdownMenuSearch,
} from "@/components/ui/dropdown-menu"
import { ChevronRight, Plus, Search, X } from "lucide-react"

interface DropdownItemProps {
  label: string
  subtitle?: string
  icon?: React.ReactNode
  onClick?: () => void
  disabled?: boolean
}

<DropdownMenu>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger className="w-full">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 border rounded-md">
      <span className="text-sm font-medium text-content-darker">Heading</span>
      <ChevronRight className="w-4 h-4 text-gray-400" />
    </div>
  </DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <DropdownMenuContent className="w-56">
    <DropdownMenuSearch>
      <div className="flex items-center px-2 py-1.5 border-b">
        <Search className="w-4 h-4 text-gray-400 mr-2" />
        <input
          type="text"
          placeholder="Search"
          className="w-full text-sm bg-transparent outline-none"
        />
      </div>
    </DropdownMenuSearch>
    <DropdownMenuGroup>
      <DropdownMenuItem>
        <Plus className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
        <span>Label</span>
      </DropdownMenuItem>
      <DropdownMenuItem className="bg-primary-lighter">
        <Plus className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
        <span>Selected Label</span>
      </DropdownMenuItem>
    </DropdownMenuGroup>
    <DropdownMenuSeparator />
    <DropdownMenuGroup>
      <DropdownMenuLabel>Heading</DropdownMenuLabel>
      <DropdownMenuItem>
        <Plus className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
        <span>Label</span>
      </DropdownMenuItem>
    </DropdownMenuGroup>
    <DropdownMenuSeparator />
    <div className="p-2">
      <button className="w-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white bg-primary rounded-md">
        CTA
      </button>
    </div>
  </DropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>
```

### Nested Dropdown
```typescript
<DropdownMenu>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger className="w-full">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 border rounded-md">
      <span className="text-sm font-medium text-content-darker">Heading</span>
      <ChevronRight className="w-4 h-4 text-gray-400" />
    </div>
  </DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <DropdownMenuContent className="w-56">
    <DropdownMenuSub>
      <DropdownMenuSubTrigger>
        <Plus className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
        <span>Label</span>
        <ChevronRight className="w-4 h-4 ml-auto" />
      </DropdownMenuSubTrigger>
      <DropdownMenuSubContent>
        <DropdownMenuItem>
          <Plus className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
          <span>Sublabel</span>
        </DropdownMenuItem>
      </DropdownMenuSubContent>
    </DropdownMenuSub>
  </DropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>
```

### Usage Guidelines
1. Use for selection menus, navigation, or action lists
2. Include search when list items exceed 10
3. Group related items with separators and labels
4. Use icons consistently for visual hierarchy
5. Include keyboard navigation support
6. Show selected state with background highlight
7. Add clear button (X) for searchable dropdowns

### Accessibility Considerations
- Use proper ARIA labels for dropdown trigger
- Implement keyboard navigation (arrows, enter, escape)
- Provide clear focus indicators
- Include screen reader descriptions
- Support type-ahead filtering when applicable

### Best Practices
1. Keep dropdown items concise
2. Use consistent icon placement
3. Implement proper loading states
4. Handle long content gracefully
5. Consider mobile interactions
6. Maintain proper z-index
7. Handle overflow properly

### Styling Guidelines
1. Use consistent spacing
2. Apply proper typography
3. Style hover states
4. Handle focus states
5. Implement proper borders
6. Consider dropdown width
